    "factor_bought_by_20mm_vs_100mm": 2.150442477876106,
    "sentence": "Carried through the reliability chain, the 100 mm by which the plate centre misses the contact centroid understates the annual failure probability by a factor of 3.6 (beta 4.24 in place of 3.94), whereas an arm known to 20 mm understates it by no more than a factor of 1.7 (beta 4.06); instrumenting the bearing to 20 mm therefore buys a factor of 2.2 on the annual failure probability the assessment reports."
